  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_0624e878c7db4cdfb0b46a6b81e0ed04",
      "statement": "The agent holds one Claude Agent SDK client open for the life of a WebSocket, replacing a per-message pattern that discarded context and ran a second inference against the raw Anthropic API purely to stream tokens; the persistent client preserves context across turns and streams tokens from the same pass that runs the tools.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/main.py#L1-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2c841b082781ac09d0de20c59bb747ae1eed064a823118c917129269bff1b5c3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/session/session.py#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7bc2496e2cca87a1a2b79857ada1f30ffe88ca5185373244004fce3de0293170:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f270fdfd5a454fa7a5c8b7d2c0b6a4f4",
      "statement": "A single session runner task owns connect and disconnect because ClaudeSDKClient.connect() enters an anyio task group and anyio requires the task that entered a scope to exit it; connecting per message and disconnecting from the WebSocket handler's finally raises RuntimeError and leaks the CLI subprocess.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/session/session.py#L13-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:028dee11acdfeaa3011b85b190e5777e616490599079a1d888cc83e6e6124344:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/session/session.py#L276-L316",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:02cd5f7233623fb02037e9819971b981d04296da1524c3c2828cfd0ae095a702:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_235bb195be70433f8f9efd002fea06d6",
      "statement": "The session is driven by four concurrent tasks — the WebSocket receive loop, the session runner, the sender task and SDK-internal tasks — where the receive loop never touches the SDK client and never awaits a turn.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/session/session.py#L13-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b0d549eee32e3123aa31e4fc98c1e05784d6d563105c26757a2491fd6dc86b0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b502519f656346ed801dba7c3b906b30",
      "statement": "Turns are serialised through a queue rather than cancelled, because cancelling a turn mid-stream leaves unread messages queued in a persistent client and those messages then interleave with the next turn's output.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/session/session.py#L29-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b34b8ffafad2158d77cfc9e652e6444578a3a0132a2e9803588d9aeb4e2fb0be:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/session/session.py#L320-L360",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d6b8c1a6fb12f79c4f975f53ccf03e44970b24c3c3d4cc4cf708f37779bf443e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d3a160b7e8cb4a9397d943a62cc028bd",
      "statement": "The WebSocket output queue is deliberately unbounded, because a bounded queue could block the permission callback before its request was transmitted, leaving nobody able to answer it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/ws_chat.py#L112-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b4179efcebbb6986c544b7326d176e219f6c70daa91dfdc272481238de284923:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_63cb252907d0414ebc0721789c79b505",
      "statement": "handle_chat queues the turn and returns immediately while all database work runs in a separate persister task, so the receive loop stays free to read the approval or interrupt that the currently running turn is waiting for.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/ws_chat.py#L269-L310",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:feb3537fde1e9ae00519d8c5d4d83d0150b9d6532ff6dedacb0c13728b1a8462:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_88681050c4cc48f5b9db757e9f1e257f",
      "statement": "The serve loop keeps one connected client until an idle timeout parks it, a reset clears the conversation, the tenant context changes, or the session closes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/session/session.py#L320-L360",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d6b8c1a6fb12f79c4f975f53ccf03e44970b24c3c3d4cc4cf708f37779bf443e:"
        }
